+"""Search Engine V2-C3: several logical paid searches, one provider start — and
+the plan, the depth, the attribution, the bytes, the budget and the resume
+semantics stay what V2-C2 made them.
+
+Under SWEEP_PAID_COMPACTION (inside V2-C2's scheduler) a contiguous run of
+compatible LinkedIn searches shares one actor start, held at the sum of their
+ceilings; every result is attributed by the source URL it names, or the run is
+refused whole; each search keeps its rows, ranks, checkpoint and done marker.
+
+NO REAL CREDENTIAL AND NO REAL CLIENT. As in V2-C2: scraper.main() in-process
+against a thread-safe scripted stand-in, _require_token patched, sockets denied.
+BatchClient extends C2's KeyedClient with the provider contract C3 relies on,
